00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:19.370
on the website.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:20.890
Tyler, you have anything to add?

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:22.530
I was going to say, can you talk about how we pretty much

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.770
have two offices that we do the pre-audit with Crawford

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:26.810
and then we do the.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.290
Yeah, so the way that things work on the state side,

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:32.010
especially with the municipalities,

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:35.210
we have a set of auditors that come in and basically close

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.090
our books for us.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.690
They do all the financial statements

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.290
and all the legwork to kind of prep it,

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.570
and then it goes to audit.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:46.490
So basically, everything is looked at double,

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.970
because we have the people that we

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:50.650
are contractually hired to help us get everything packaged

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.770
together, and then we have an actual external set

00:05:53.770 --> 00:06:02.100
of auditors that come in and look at everything.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.580
Is that something we're required to do,

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.940
or is that just something we do?

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.340
I don't think it's a requirement.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:09.500
I think it's very common in Oklahoma for it to be that way.

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:12.540
The last conversation that I had with our auditors about it

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:17.220
is their audit firm will not even go out to bid an audit

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:20.740
unless this package deal kind of happens before.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:23.620
So it's not an actual state stature or anything

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:24.700
that we have to do that.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.580
It's just kind of common in Oklahoma

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.820
that you have some prep work done before.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:32.180
It just cleans everything up before it actually goes to audit.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.860
I know those audits also posted.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:34.360
Yes.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:44.550
Anyone in the community can go look at them.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.430
Chris, there's been some questions

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:49.550
come up recently about the number of transfers we're doing.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.590
Can you touch on some of the reason

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.590
why we do the transfers we do and how all that works?

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:55.470
Sure.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.710
So a lot of the transfers, if you

00:06:57.710 --> 00:06:59.070
will look at this box right here,

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.990
it explains a lot of what happens.

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:05.830
So MSUA is paying back rainy day fund to build that nest egg.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:10.110
MSUA supports part of it.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.350
There's multiple transfers that happen.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:15.670
So that's why it gets complicated.

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:18.910
MSUA pays on bonds and then there's

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.790
sales tax money that was pledged for those bonds.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.870
So there are actual city sales tax money

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:26.790
have to be ran through MSUA and then transferred back

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.430
to the city to meet those bond requirements.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.910
So it makes that number look really inflated

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.110
because you send all the sales tax over

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.670
and then you send the majority of it back.

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:38.310
There's some that doesn't come back.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.150
It stays over there on that side,

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.550
but the majority of it comes back.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:44.950
So out of the 14 million or so transfers,

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:47.790
like almost 8 million of that is just,

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:50.350
it's basically just being washed through MSUA

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:52.150
and coming right back to the city.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.310
And then it funds some other things.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:59.430
Street Natalie, like I said, gets 500,000.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.110
It's paying some electron improvement bonds.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:05.830
The fiber and AMI loan is transferred out and paid.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:06.990
What else?

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:10.590
115,000 goes to the airport taxiway relocation grant.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.630
That's something for that.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.790
It's also supported MDRA in the form of Coleman.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:17.950
Let's see.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.670
I think those are the major ones.

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:24.390
Did I miss anything, Jill?

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.230
Thank you.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:40.340
Yep.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:41.380
Anybody have any questions?

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:44.380
Any other questions?

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:45.220
I don't have any questions,

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:47.540
but based on the information

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.420
and the questions that I've had from the community,

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.060
I wanna recommend that we table this

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.220
until our next council meeting

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.260
so that we have more time to go through it,

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.140
be more thorough and answer some of the questions

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:56.980
that are being proposed.

00:08:56.980 --> 00:08:58.140
Absolutely, I agree.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:58.980
I think.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:00.340
I'm available anytime.

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:02.020
I think that would be best if there's any.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:02.860
Okay.

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:05.940
And then I look forward to your deep dive

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:06.780
into the presentation,

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.980
so it probably will answer some of those questions.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:09.820
Sure.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.020
That's my recommendation.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.980
I don't know how everybody else feels, but I agree.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.460
Agreed.

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:16.300
Thank you, guys.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.140
Thank you.

